1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,200
In 1943 the Soviet Union built twenty-nine thousand tanks.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,400
Germany built twelve thousand.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:13,600
The gap was not a matter of courage, and everyone on both sides knew it.

4
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,900
It was a matter of factories, and the factories were still standing.

5
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:22,400
Nobody wrote any of it down at the time.

6
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:29,800
The men who kept the counts were told the numbers were a state secret, and most of them died believing it.

7
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:36,200
What survives is a ledger in Chelyabinsk, four hundred pages long, in one clerk's handwriting.

8
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:42,000
Seventy percent of the Soviet tank fleet came off the lines in that single year.
